@----------------------------------------
@node DECLARATIONS
@prev BUILD
@next INSTALLING
@toc INDEX
@{h1}Declarations.

There are variable declarations, function definitions, and  function
prototypes.

Variable types include scalar types (char, byte, int), arrays (e.g. int[10]),
and pointers (e.g. int*).

@{h2}Control Structures.
You'll find the usual control constructs: if-else, while, and for loops, as
well as statements such as break, continue, and return.

@{h2}Inline Assembly.
A special asm block can be used to embed raw Z80N assembly 
code inside functions.

@{h2}I/O Primitives.
For basic output, built-in functions putc() and puts() are 
provided.

Along with nextreg() and readreg().

@{h2}Banks.
A bank construct allows you to group a statement block into a memory bank
